  "description": "Demolition of an existing detached garage and side extension, erection of a single storey front porch, side and rear wraparound extension. First floor rear extension with juliet balcony.\r",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "By reason of scale, mass and design, the proposed first floor extension would appear as a dominant and incongruous addition to the host dwelling, eroding the symmetry shared with the adjoining dwelling, resulting in unacceptable impacts on the character and appearance of the host property and streetscape, conflicting with Policies D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the Council's Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate through the submission of cogent information that the proposed extension would not have an adverse impact on the closest ground floor principal habitable room windows at No. 61 Highdown in terms of a loss of daylight and sunlight. Given the scale of the extension and the proximity of neighbouring windows, it is considered that there is a likelihood that the development would reduce light entering into the neighbouring habitable room, which in turn would harm the residential amenities of the occupants of the neighbouring property.  The excessive depth of the proposed extension would also result in an overbearing and undue sense of enclosure to No. 61 Highdown. The proposal is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
